        "justification": "The pattern exposes, on the smallest latent bow, both the supported state-specific formula branch and an exact-support rational NONID branch.",
        "gap": "Ordinary ID gives only bow failure. Chen--Darwiche Theorem 15 elimination of \\(D\\), under its separability and parent conditions, leaves the bow, and Theorem 18 assumes \\(C_V=\\{\\Pr(X)>0:X\\text{ is a treatment variable}\\}\\); neither theorem separates the supported and unsupported intervention values on this declared structural-zero face. Chen--Darwiche's 2026 Theorems 1--2 are sound identification results for CSI and state-alphabet constraints under strict observational positivity, not a completeness or exact-support countermodel result for a valid treatment state assigned zero observational mass.",
